{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "曜日（よーび）[Days of the Week]",
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            },
            {
              "type": "underline"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Okinawan traditionally did not have days of the week. Therefore, most of it is loaned from Japanese.",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Days of the week to memorize and do not change much across regions:",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "日曜日（にちよーび）= Sunday",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "火曜日（くゎよーび）= Tuesday",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Other days of the week that may depend on the region (and is still highly debated on by individual):",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "月曜日（じちよーび）= Monday",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "水曜日（しーよーび）= Wednesday",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "木曜日（むくよーび）= Thursday",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "金曜日（ちんよーび）= Friday",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "土曜日（(っ)んちゃよーび）= Saturday",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Some people might write よーび as ようび, but the pronunciation stays the same, but it's just orthography choice, since Okinawan was traditionally a spoken language.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
